As the Lady of the Lake, for many years, Nimue resided in the [[Crystal Caves]], with Vivian and their bodyguards, [[Mallory]] and [[White]]. {{source|Cave of the Casterwills}}

When the [[Huntik Foundation]] team came to England on the trail of the [[Willblade]], [[Sophie Casterwill]] and [[LeBlanche]] met Nimue and Vivian deep in the crystal caves. Abiding by Casterwill law, Nimue tested Sophie and tasked her with recovering the [[Amulet]] of [[Sorcerel]]. After Sophie succeeded, Nimue called off [[Mallory]] and [[White]] from their attack on [[Lok Lambert]], [[Dante Vale]], and [[Zhalia Moon]] and agreed to help them on their quest to find Avalon. {{source|Cave of the Casterwills}} 

After the arrival of [[the Organization]], Nimue showed the team to the cliff face where the Dragon's Breath could be formed. However, she was interrupted by two [[Suits]] who threatened to open fire on her unless given access to cross the bridge. As the two Suits fell through the Dragon's Breath, Nimue reminded the team that it was only a guide and not a physical bridge. As the team departed to follow the light to Avalon, Nimue wished them luck and sent her Titan, [[Undine]], to protect their boat. {{source|Knight of the Willblade}}

Upon the activation of the [[Blue Star]] by Dante's team, Nimue and Vivian gazed at the star in amazement from the coast of England. {{source|The Titan in the Temple of Sun}}

Nimue led the Casterwill meeting at the [[Fortress of Iron Will]], where she voiced her unconditional support for Sophie and her idea of an offensive strike against the [[Blood Spiral]] despite the disapproval of [[Focauld Casterwill]] and the [[Rune Guardian|Rue Guardians]], who opted to go back into hiding. After Sophie embarked on a quest to obtain [[Mythras]], the Legendary Titan of Valor, and to claim leadership of the Casterwills, Nimue questioned why Lucas was so harsh towards Sophie. {{source|Sophie on Trial}}
[[File:S2E40 Nimue Sacroblaze.png|thumb|170px|Nimue sacrifices herself to stop the Blood Spirals]]
When the [[Blood Spiral]] army attacked the Fortress, Nimue fought alongside Sophie, [[LeBlanche]], and [[Santiago]] at the top of the cliffs. After Sophie and LeBlanche were overpowered, Nimue used all her power, using [[Soulburn]] to protect the Casterwill meeting giving the Rue Guradians and Focauld enough time to activate the Legendary Power to protect the Fortress. She later died using the [[Sacroblade]] spell. With her dying breath, Nimue encouraged Sophie, telling her not to fear her future, allowing Sophie to regain her confidence, powerbond with [[Sorcerel]] and invoke the Titan of Valor, Mythras. Following the end of the battle, a grieving Vivian took on Nimue's role of the Lady of the Lake. {{source|The Spiral War}}

[[File:S2E30 Nimue summons Undine.jpg|thumb|180px|Nimue summons [[Undine the Water Spirit]]]]
As a Casterwill elder, Nimue possessed many of the spells of the ancient Casterwill tomes and could open portals within the Crystal Caves. Like [[Sophie Casterwill]], she was to able to mentally sense magical forces, like the energy of [[Sabriel]]. {{source|Cave of the Casterwills}} In addition, her favored Titan [[Undine the Water Spirit]] possessed a range water based abilities. {{source|Knight of the Willblade}}
